WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.930
Your build robot has admin rights on the whole cluster.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.665
One leaked token, and an attacker owns every namespace.

3
00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:12.515
This port has two guards: access control, and pod security.

4
00:00:12.535 --> 00:00:14.775
First: who can do what, and where?

5
00:00:14.795 --> 00:00:17.175
A role is a list of verbs on resources.

6
00:00:17.195 --> 00:00:19.860
For example: get and list pods.

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.745
A binding gives that role to a user or a service account.

8
00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:25.195
There is no deny rule.

9
00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:27.920
What you did not grant is denied.

10
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.280
Second: what may a container do?

11
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.818
By default, many images run as root.

12
00:00:32.838 --> 00:00:35.115
A break-out is then much worse.

13
00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:40.375
So run as a normal user, block privilege escalation, and drop capabilities.

14
00:00:40.395 --> 00:00:45.725
A label on the namespace makes the cluster reject pods that break these rules.

15
00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.810
Quick recap of security.

16
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.172
Grant small roles.

17
00:00:49.192 --> 00:00:50.860
Nothing is allowed by default.

18
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.720
And do not run as root.

19
00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.840
Now start the first lesson below.
